  "observations": [
    "B-COLD-RE-DERIVE performed the required session/resource/endpoint discovery and succeeded on 40/40 held-out test tasks (success_rate=1.0 at novelty 0.0, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75 in both families F1 and F2).",
    "B-RETRIEVAL-SHAPED (top-K=3 structural similarity plus mandatory discovery) succeeded on 40/40 held-out test tasks (success_rate=1.0 at every novelty level).",
    "T-SPIDER-PARAM resolved EXECUTABLE via the audited kernel on 40/40 held-out tasks (no fallback), retrieval_calls=1, repair_attempts=0, success_rate=1.0.",
    "Across deterministic counters (http_requests+retrieval_calls+verification_calls+repair_attempts) per success, treatment equals cold at novelty 0.25/0.5/0.75 (4/4, 5/5, 6/6) and is worse at novelty 0.0 (4 vs 2).",
    "The frozen latency-inclusive cost_per_success yields a treatment 'advantage' over cold of roughly 1e-4 to 9e-4 at novelty 0.25/0.5/0.75 (bases 4-6 units, <0.02%), which is within the latency noise floor; on counters only the treatment ties cold.",
    "T-SPIDER-PARAM cost_per_success is below B-RETRIEVAL-SHAPED by 2 counter units at every novelty level, driven entirely by retrieval_calls (treatment=1 vs retrieval=3), not by any http_requests saving.",
    "B-EMPTIED-REGISTRY matched B-COLD-RE-DERIVE to within 7.6e-5 relative difference at every point.",
    "B-LITERAL-KERNEL returned EXPLORE on all 200 held-out tasks (success_rate=0.0), because literal mechanism confidence 0.5 is below min_confidence 0.8.",
    "PC-EXACT-REPLAY succeeded on 20/20 training tasks (success_rate=1.0).",
    "D-DIRECT-NO-DISCOVERY (diagnostic): 10/10 success at novelty 0.0, 0/10 at novelty 0.5, 0/10 at novelty 0.75.",
    "Known-negative cases: 30/30 refused with bound_action=null and a correctly categorized reason (refusal_rate=1.0, reason_correctness=1.0).",
    "Design-level dynamic-range certificate computed before arm execution is false; observed certificate after the run is also false.",
    "model_calls=0 and model_tokens=0 for every arm (credential-free localhost stdlib HTTP)."
  ],
  "validity_notes": [
    "FREEZE-GATE DEFECT: spec.json / prereg.md state the pre-freeze certificate is enforced by the freeze script reading spec.json.dynamic_range_certified. scripts/freeze_experiment.py does not read that key (its required-key list omits it) and no reference to 'dynamic_range' exists anywhere under scripts/ or .github/; spec.json contains no dynamic_range_certified field. freeze.json therefore exists for a packet whose C1 certificate is false. The certificate was recomputed here from the frozen task bank plus frozen arm capabilities with no run data and is false.",
    "CLASSIFICATION: the frozen OVERALL rule lists both FALSIFIES ('C1 fails (certificate unsatisfiable)') and MEASUREMENT_INVALID ('C1 fails at freeze time (certificate=false)'). The gate never ran at freeze time, and this run produced valid, reproducible, deterministic measurements; the contract states a valid scientific negative is normally status=COMPLETE with a negative outcome. Therefore status=COMPLETE/outcome=FALSIFIES (bounded substrate-class negative) was chosen. The parent experiment EXP-PRODUCT-37982016598 encoded the analogous situation as MEASUREMENT_INVALID; an auditor may prefer that convention. All raw facts are preserved so the DIRECTOR can reclassify without re-running.",
    "C3 PASS is not a substantive advantage. The frozen cost metric includes latency_ms/1000, which is continuous instrument noise; the treatment 'wins' at novelty 0.5/0.75 by 5e-4..9e-4 on a 5-6 unit base. On deterministic counters only, treatment ties cold exactly (C3_counter_only=false). Do not read C3 as evidence of work compression.",
    "SUBSTRATE DESIGN WORKAROUNDS (documented per prereg section 8 support-boundary mitigation): discovered identifiers and the given target_value were kept inside the support grammar the kernel induces from training. Without the value workaround, the audited kernel's support predicate refuses the given value slot and the treatment falls back to cold on every task. These choices do not affect the certificate or the top-level outcome; they give the treatment its best shot.",
    "MEASUREMENT ISOLATION: the audited kernel blob was vendored byte-identically and the shipped src/spider/kernel.py was not modified, so the shipped-kernel regression (blob cfec9866 lacking the parameterized path) is disclosed but out of scope for this run.",
    "Latency was measured with time.perf_counter over localhost; structural counters are deterministic under SEED=42 but latency_ms varies run to run.",
    "The substrate uses a single-threaded stdlib http.server on an ephemeral localhost port; no external network, credentials, browser or model calls were used.",
    "C2 ('all arms >= 0.80') is evaluated over the four main arms (T-SPIDER-PARAM, B-COLD-RE-DERIVE, B-RETRIEVAL-SHAPED, B-EMPTIED-REGISTRY). B-LITERAL-KERNEL is the causal-ablation control that C9 requires to be < 0.20, so it cannot also be a C2 arm without contradicting C9; PC-EXACT-REPLAY and D-DIRECT-NO-DISCOVERY are controls/diagnostic."
  ],
  "unresolved": [
